description:
Read the signed facts at a canonical address (cell64). When a band has no fact yet but has a registered materializer, the responder fetches it. A fact_cid names one signed attestation, so you can cite a fact and verify it again. Resolve the cid anywhere and you get the same bytes. A fact_cid is NOT a fingerprint of the observation. The digest includes the responder's key and the time it signed. Thus two responders that measure the same thing make different fact_cids, and a cid resolves only at the responder that signed it. For identity across responders, use emem_entity. Send `deterministic:true` (or a `provenance` class list) to keep only facts that you can compute from the cited raw source. In the memory algebra this is ensure(cell, bands), not get: you state what must exist.

When to use: Call this after `emem_locate`, or with a cell64 or a place name. It returns every Primary fact at that (cell, band, tslot). A band can have no fact but have a materializer. Then the responder fetches the upstream value, signs it, stores it and returns it in the same call. The first call is slow; later calls use the cache. Thus any wired band recalls at any cell on Earth: send `bands: [<band>]`. `materialize_notes` lists what the call fetched. Empty notes mean no materializer here.

Example arguments: {"cell":"defi.zb64a.cAzU.zfa27","bands":["weather.temperature_2m","copdem30m.elevation_mean"]}
